        "original_id": "d814144a-96cb-5a25-9eb6-fa316a8e8159",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Constantine Orbelian, Lili Chookasian, Dmitry Hvorostovsky\n- Products: Where Are You My Brothers?\n- Companies: Delos Productions\n- Topics: classical music, opera, World War II songs\n\nFacts:\n- Lili Chookasian was born on August 1, 1921, and she became an American contralto who appeared with many major symphony orchestras and opera houses worldwide.\n- Constantine Garrievich Orbelian, Jr. was born in San Francisco on August 27, 1956, and he is an American conductor and pianist of Armenian and Russian descent.\n- Where Are You My Brothers? is a 2003 album of Russian-language World War II songs recorded by baritone Dmitry Hvorostovsky and conductor Constantine Orbelian for Delos Productions.\n- Lili Chookasian died on April 9, 2012.",
